n dany helps the new  mutants save sunspot from the hellfire  thugs  some of those thugs have felt  wolverine's claws in the past  so dany pulls an image of logan from  their mind and projects it onto reality  making them think he's attacking them  again but that's about  it and even this power is limited she  can't just create any random image that  she imagines  however under professor x's tutelage the  boundaries of dany's powers expand  in 1983's new mutants number four dany  shows that she could manifest the image  of someone's greatest desire  when she pulls from a teen boy's mind  the image of him passionately kissing  the teacher he has a crush on  eventually she's able to empathically  produce images besides those connected  to such extreme emotions  she also discovers a much more offensive  use for her powers  dany can focus her psychic energy into  so-called psychic arrows  appearing as arrows of energy or fire  the missile weapons can mentally stun  her targets  or even cause them to relive past trauma  the new mutants don't have many of their  own villains and most of what you might  call their rogues gallery  is culled from the larger x-men mythos  but one notable exception  is the demon bear whose introduction to  new mutants marked a whole new visual  era for the team's stories  among other things new mutants  co-creator chris claremont  is known for dropping hints towards  future stories and letting them simmer  for a while  before eventually bringing them center  stage the demon bear is a perfect  example of this  as he makes an appearance in dany's  dreams in 1983's new mutants number  three but doesn't strike until the end  of 1984's new mutants number 17.  the demon bear is a dark and powerful  spirit from a dimension called the  badlands  who feeds on his victim's negative  emotions before she joins the new  mutants  dany believes her parents were killed by  this bear but at the end of new mutants  number 20  she is tearfully reunited with them  having discovered they were enslaved  and transformed into the demon bear  itself when they're separated from demon  bear by magic's  soul sword dany believes her war with  the spirit is over  unfortunately the demon bear returns in  a number of subsequent volumes of  x-force  to haunt and battle mirage while most  people associate asgard with characters  such as thor the other worldly realm is  also linked to characters outside of  marvel's norse mythology  for example a fan favorite x-men new  mutants crossover from 1985 called the  asgardian wars had a huge impact on the  x mythos  particularly when it came to mirage in  league with loki the enchantress  transports the new mutants to different  parts of the ten realms  and dany finds herself in valhalla home  of the honored dead  while there she saves a winged horse  from a group of hunters and that act has  more  significant consequences than she could  have ever imagined likely due to her  empathic powers  dany bonds with the horse whom she names  brightwind  and that bond makes her a member of the  valkrior  these are hela's valkyries whose task in  ancient norse myth  was to choose who would die on the  battlefield i think it's great that  there is a  an elite force of women warriors  it's about time while most of her  teammates noticed nothing different  about her at first  the asgardians are visibly intimidated  by dany  and the alien warlock attacks her when  he first sees her when she returns to  earth at the end of the crossover she  retains her connection to the valkyrie  and brings brightwind home with her one  of the results of her connection to the  valkyrie art  is that mirage suffers premonitions when  someone is about to die  in the form of death spirits that only  she can see hovering over the victim  when the new mutants are formed they're  students of professor x  eventually however xavier puts a  temporarily reformed magneto in charge  of his school  but in the field and in the danger room  